        "link": "https://www.france24.com/en/gaza-s-evacuated-premature-babies-return-to-devastated-strip",
        "orario": "11:44",
        "timestamp": 1774950256,
        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. Gaza's evacuated premature babies return to devastated strip Middle East Issued on: 31/03/2026 - 11:44 Modified: 31/03/2026 - 11:49 Eleven children born prematurely, who were later evacuated to Egypt during the war, have returned to Gaza. The children were moved in the first weeks of the conflict when the hospital where they were being cared for was besieged by the Israeli military. The return to their families has been marked by uncertainty in a Gaza Strip devastated by two and a half years of war. Vital desalination plant in the Gulf become war targets 31/03/2026 Middle East Syria's al-Sharaa visits Germany to discuss refugee return, war and recovery 31/03/2026 Middle East Three UN peacekeepers in Lebanon killed in 24 hours 31/03/2026 Middle East 31/03/2026 Middle East 'The Houthis hold serious cards' expert says, amid threats to choke off Red Sea passage 30/03/2026 Middle East Trump's options in Iran range from bad to worse 30/03/2026 Middle East UK ex-ambassador Westmacott warns: Whether PM likes it or not, British govt 'a bit involved' in Iran 30/03/2026 Middle East Kyiv useful to US, Gulf at critical time: Drone interceptors 'more effective than Patriot missiles' 30/03/2026 Middle East While Trump vows Iran deal on the way, 'evidence points to another direction' 30/03/2026 Middle East"
